course: dictionary
lesson: 7303
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pitcher can mean a jug for pouring drinks, a player in baseball, or a plant with jug-shaped leaves. The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Pitcher plants have jug-shaped leaves with slippery rims and a pool of digestive liquid; insects come for nectar, slip in and drown.» The words jug-shaped, insects and liquid show that this pitcher is a plant, not a jug you pour from.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about: maths, sport or nature? Choose the meaning that fits that topic. Then check it by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A pitcher is a large jug with a handle and a lip for pouring drinks such as water, milk or juice.
fact: In baseball and softball, the pitcher is the player who throws the ball to the batter.
fact: A pitcher plant has jug-shaped leaves that trap and digest insects.
fact: «Pitcher plants trap insects that slip down the walls into the liquid, where they are digested.» Digested means broken down so the plant can use it.
fact: «Little pitchers have big ears» is an old saying. It means children hear more than adults think.
exercise: «Pitcher plants have jug-shaped leaves with slippery rims.» What is a pitcher in this sentence? | *A plant with jug-shaped leaves that traps insects | A large jug with a handle for pouring | A person who throws a ball
exercise: Sam says, «The pitcher threw a fast ball to the batter in the last inning.» What does pitcher mean? | A plant that eats insects | A large jug for pouring water | *The player who throws the ball to the batter
exercise: «She filled the pitcher with two litres of cold milk.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | *A large jug with a lip for pouring | A plant with slippery leaves | A baseball player who throws the ball
test: «The pitcher on the kitchen table was full of cold lemonade.» What does pitcher mean here? | A plant that traps insects in its leaves | *A large jug for pouring drinks | A player who throws the ball
test: «Little pitchers have big ears» is an old saying. What does it mean? | *Children hear more than adults think | Small jugs can hold big drinks | Baseball players need good hearing
exam: In «pitcher plants are slippery water slides into a pool of juice», what is a pitcher plant? | *A plant that traps insects in a slippery pool | A player who slides into base | A large jug used to pour juice
